    <!-- Feature Grid -->
    <section class="section">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-header">
          <div class="eyebrow">Foundation</div>
          <h2 class="section-heading">Built on a single<br/>architectural decision.</h2>
          <p class="section-sub">Shadow DOM solves encapsulation. Voidable solves the opposite problem: components that are deliberately transparent to their environment.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-grid">
          <div class="feature-card">
            <div class="feature-card-title">Light DOM rendering</div>
            <p class="feature-card-desc">No Shadow DOM barrier. Your CSS reaches into every component without ::part() incantations.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="feature-card">
            <div class="feature-card-title">Knob-driven theming</div>
            <p class="feature-card-desc">A dozen inputs derive every token. Set them on the page, or on any subtree, and everything inside follows.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="feature-card">
            <div class="feature-card-title">Federation-ready</div>
            <p class="feature-card-desc">Singleton-safe customElements.define(). Same library loads once across federated modules.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="feature-card">
            <div class="feature-card-title">Embedded-grade bundles</div>
            <p class="feature-card-desc">Pairs with Solid + UnoCSS for bundle sizes that are IoT friendly. Tree-shakes to component-level granularity, or use the autoloader to fetch only the components a page uses.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="feature-card">
            <div class="feature-card-title">Agent-friendly markup</div>
            <p class="feature-card-desc">Semantic void-* custom elements with reflected attributes. Stable selectors for Playwright, AI agents, screen readers. In development, the console says what a wrong attribute, value or child silently did, so the agent that wrote it can fix it.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="feature-card">
            <div class="feature-card-title">Accessible by derivation</div>
            <p class="feature-card-desc">Contrast floors, focus rings, reduced motion and forced colours hold for every theme, because they are part of the formulas.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

